module

public import Theory.SpecificGroups.ReeF4.MaximalSubgroups.CommutingComponents.CarrierIdentification.Basic

/-!
# The concrete normalizer calculation for a Suzuki factor

The standard subgroup is the actual exceptional fixed intersection of the
full signed middle-node B₂ Levi, defined in `CarrierIdentification.Basic`.
The remaining calculation bounds its normalizer **in the Ree group** by the
square of the Suzuki order. It concerns the full subgroup normalizer, not
the torus normalizer generated by subsystem Weyl words.

Once a supplied component is conjugated to this Levi, its commuting partner
and the two supplied carrier equivalences already give that many elements
in the relative normalizer. Thus only this upper bound is needed; no order
or simplicity theorem for the ambient Ree group is requested here.

This definition records an unproved geometric obligation. The maximal-subgroup
list alone does not prove the bound for this particular embedded Levi.
Source context: Malle, J. Algebra 139 (1991), 52--69,
DOI 10.1016/0021-8693(91)90283-E; the Suzuki-wreath entry reproduced in
the proof of Theorem 5 of arXiv:0910.4758, pp.2--3.
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace ReeF4.MaximalSubgroups.CommutingComponents.FactorNormalizer

open Subgroup BenderSuzuki.MatrixGroups CarrierIdentification

/-- The required upper bound for the ambient normalizer of the concrete
fixed B₂ Levi, with the simple-family parameter range retained. -/
def StandardLeviNormalizerCardBound : Prop :=
  ∀ m, 1 ≤ m →
    Nat.card (normalizer (standardSuzukiLevi m : Set (Model m))) ≤
      Nat.card (SuzukiMatrixGroup m) ^ 2

end ReeF4.MaximalSubgroups.CommutingComponents.FactorNormalizer
